# Banter in Skitterdeep Mine (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is skitterdeep_mine): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ sk_hills_trail_01_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:sk_hills_trail and not flag.sk_arrived
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the ruts under the hornbeam, Lucan, every tiny centipede in the mud is marching one way like the house just called last bets.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A disciplined column, Silas, though I can only award them a four out of ten for spoor discipline across a wet wagon track.
interject name:silas_vane: Your little Barnaby isn't grading them, friend, he's eyeing that rotted saddle bag in the brambles like it owes him cheese.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A gentleman's hound does not rummage through unclaimed luggage, Silas, however dark these beeches grow.
interject name:silas_vane: Tell's in the twitch, and right now my ribs say whatever called those crawlers uphill is holding a stacked shoe.
endif
-> END

~ sk_camp_02_rook_tobin
if name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and at:sk_camp and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unfenced square shaft, sagging headframe timber, and green gas rising straight into the yard without a vent flue. Shocking neglect of parish code, Tobin.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Never mind the timber, Rook, someone painted Skitterdeep right over Glitterdeep on that warehouse sign, and bad naming is how rot gets a taproot.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Painting over two letters without filing a variance is a municipal offence, and leaving a tipped ore cart in the road is another.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep that turnip lantern steady by the drift mouth, the green damp coming up those iron rungs smells like a cellar that forgot how to drain.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Settle down now, I will log the rusted hanging chain on the docket, provided you remind me to draw breath before we climb down.
endif
-> END

~ sk_upper_03_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_upper and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Rotten timbering, overturned carts, and a heap of gold and gems sitting twenty paces from a pile of loose organs. Terrible staging, Cordelia, no sense of billing.
interject name:cordelia_skein: On the contrary, Delphine, the eye hanging by its optic nerve over the Crosscut shows a remarkably steady hand with tissue suspension.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He says the silver chalices are tarnished on the bias, and frankly the smell of old meat coming up the lift shaft is ruining my velvet.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Fascinating pathology, though, how the humidity from thirty feet down preserves the humours while the silks beside the coins are already spotting with mould.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Do not touch a single jewel until we know who left their liver in the cheap seats.
endif
-> END

~ sk_machine_shop_04_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_machine_shop and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Cordelia, this middle room smells of dead horse and sour grease, and someone has made a bed out of rotted wine-red surcoats.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look at the dust by the winch drum, Lucan, the handprints between the two doors have a most irregular span across the knuckles.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Sloppy posture on the approach, if you please, and they left a perfectly serviceable maul under a tarp while burying a dungeoneer's pack in rubbish.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The green gas leaking through the warped boards is coating the ruined tools on the rack, I would love to assay a scraping.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Take your specimen quickly, then, for Barnaby has flattened his ears at that horse blanket, and I do not care for how my own throat is rumbling.
endif
-> END

~ sk_warehouse_05_silas_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_warehouse and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Smashed shelves, rubble to the ankle, and somebody's still snoring in the green haze like they paid rent on the floor. Bad odds in this store, Cordelia.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Notice the barrel of rotted flour by the crates, Silas, the tiny centipedes have colonized the meal at an admirably uniform ratio.
interject name:silas_vane: Yeah, well, they can keep the flour and the rusted sheet metal, I'm reading the chalk on this half-legible foreman's board to see who's still on the tab.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Do hold still by that rotted lunch pail, darling, your smaller shadow is lagging a full step behind you in the cobwebs.
interject name:silas_vane: Leave the shade alone, when you hear heavy breathing in a wrecked room and nobody wakes up, you keep your bone cards palmed.
endif
-> END

~ sk_deep_06_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_upper and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Sinew knotted into the floor slabs and a ring of entrails sweating yellow-green gas across the thoroughfare. There is no zoning in the north that permits a wall of slick flesh, Cordelia.
interject name:cordelia_skein: All six of my eyes just clicked at once, Rook, the vascular calibration holding that bronze door to the living tissue is exquisite.
interject name:rook_coldwake: The wall squirmed when I checked the plumb line, and the centipedes are thick as spilled rice around the foot of the shaft.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Hear the water trickling in the dark behind the green-purple pulse, the whole drift is circulating like an opened thorax.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Mind the turf by those sigils, then, my knuckles are going soft enough in this damp without stepping in an unlicensed laboratory.
endif
-> END

~ sk_camp_07_silas_rook
if name:silas_vane and name:rook_coldwake and at:sk_camp and flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Funny how a place looks when the bank's broken, Rook, same sagging timber and rusted rail, but the chill in my ribs finally folded its hand.
interject name:rook_coldwake: The square shaft is still breathing green gas into the yard, Silas, though the draught coming off the ridge has lost its grease.
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the kennel yard there, an old doghouse and a numbered brass collar in the weeds, and nobody left to whistle at the end of the shift.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Numbered brass is proper parish registry, at least, better than leaving a watchman's name to wash off the warehouse sign.
interject name:silas_vane: Come on, sit on that flat stone at the camp's edge and take a breath for the shift log, friend, we cleared the table.
endif
-> END
